# A test file is an outside consumer of its module (gavel 2026-10-12), so a
# private name is refused. Read straight from a test constant it is:
#   test_x = twice 2 == 4   ->   error[name]: unknown name `twice`
# Read from inside a helper function in the test file, it is not.
#
# Run: kanso test priv
#
# Should: refuse at check with error[name]: unknown name `twice`.
#
# Does: compiles and runs, and the test fails at run time with
#   error[runtime]: unknown name `~twice`
#     --> priv/priv_test.kso:15:3
# naming an internal, mangled spelling of the private function.
fn helper x
  twice x

test_private = helper 2 == 4
